d/Split Screen Co-op","PvP","Steam Achievements","Steam Cloud","Remote Play on TV","Steam Trading Cards","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"controller":"full","dev":["Locomalito","Gryzor87","Abylight Barcelona"],"pub":["Abylight Studios"],"released":"Sep 20, 2017","meta":82,"langs":["English","French","Italian","German","Spanish - Spain","Japanese","Russian","Turkish","Simplified Chinese"],"min":[["OS","Windows Vista, 7, 8 o 10"],["Processor","1GHz+"],["Memory","512 MB RAM"],["Graphics","128 MB"],["Storage","175 MB available space"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Bio-mechanical Meroptians bent on conquest have invaded the Omios star, and you fly the Delta Lance against them in a horizontal shoot 'em up. The game offers 21 levels split into 35 sublevels with a choice of route, plus weapons and power-ups to pick in each mission. Expect over 100 enemies, 35 bosses and hazards beyond bullets.\n\nThe design draws on classic shmups, with retro-styled art, an optional CRT monitor effect and a soundtrack of more than 60 tracks. You can play solo or in shared-screen co-op, and there is a Robot Chase spin-off. It suits genre fans who want a hard game with secrets, multiple endings and rankings."}}